    {
      "title": "Use of Proceeds",
      "excerpt": "USE OF PROCEEDS We will retain broad discretion\nover the use of the net proceeds from the sale of the securities offered hereby. We intend to use the net proceeds from the sale of securities\nwe offer as indicated in the applicable prospectus supplement, information incorporated by reference, or free writing prospectus. Field: Page; Sequence: 82; Value: 1 Field: Sequence; Type: Arabic; Name: PageNo 35 Field: /Sequence Field: /Page DIVIDENDS\nAND DIVIDEND POLICY Intercont\u2019s board of directors has discretion\non whether to distribute dividends, subject to certain restrictions under Cayman Islands law. In addition, Intercont\u2019s shareholders\nmay by ordinary resolution declare a dividend, but no dividend may exceed the amount recommended by its board of directors.\u00a0In either\ncase, all dividends are subject to certain restrictions under Cayman Islands law, namely that Intercont may only pay dividen",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dilution",
      "excerpt": "DILUTION Our\nhistorical net tangible book value on December 31, 2025 was US$24.6 million, or US$101.2 per Ordinary Share. \u201cNet tangible book\nvalue\u201d is total assets minus the sum of liabilities and intangible assets. \u201cNet tangible book value per share\u201d is net\ntangible book value divided by the total number of shares outstanding. Because we have a dual-class share structure, net tangible book\nvalue per share is calculated based on the aggregate number of Class A Ordinary Shares and Class B Ordinary Shares outstanding, being\n3,118,524.04 Ordinary Shares on a pro forma basis and 18,118,524.04 Ordinary Shares on a pro forma as adjusted basis. After\ngiving effect to the pro forma adjustments described under \u201cCapitalization\u201d and to the sale of the 15,000,000 Class A Ordinary\nShares in this offering, at an offering price of US$1.30 per Class A Ordinary Share, after deducting estimated offering e",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    }
  ],
